Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 04:40:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm8350: keep PCIe GDSCs in retention during
 suspend

The Qualcomm PCIe controller driver keeps the link up across system
suspend when an endpoint is present (Wi-Fi on PCIe0 here), so its power
domain must not be switched off. With PWRSTS_OFF_ON, genpd powers off
pcie_0_gdsc in the noirq phase of suspend-to-idle and the SoC
cold-resets there (traced with a step marker in PMIC SDAM: last step
"noirq power domain" of 1c00000.pcie).

Do what SM8450, SM8550 and SC8280XP already do and let the PCIe GDSCs
only go to retention. s2idle now survives and resumes with Wi-Fi.

---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8350.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8350.c
@@ -3421,7 +3421,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_0_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc pcie_1_gdsc = {
@@ -3429,7 +3429,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_1_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc ufs_card_gdsc = {
